# Web Performance

## Defaults

Lazy loading, code splitting, image optimization, responsive images, caching, minimal JavaScript, font optimization, compression.

## Measure before optimizing

Track LCP, CLS, INP, TTFB, bundle size, image weight, request count.
Record lab evidence in `docs/seo/TECHNICAL-SEO-AUDIT.md` and `docs/qa/VERIFICATION-LOG.md`.
Do not claim Perf gains without before/after numbers.

## Critical content

Do not lazy-load above-the-fold content that harms comprehension or accessibility.
LCP candidates (hero image/video poster, primary headline block) use priority / eager loading where Next Image supports it.

## Migration performance baseline

Record current site performance metrics during audit in `docs/seo/TECHNICAL-SEO-AUDIT.md`.
New site must meet or exceed baseline scores.

## Images (UI)

- Prefer `next/image` with explicit width/height or `fill` + sized parent.
- Modern formats (WebP, AVIF where the pipeline supports them).
- Responsive `sizes` for grid/hero layouts.
- Do not ship multi-megabyte PNGs for decorative or below-fold UI when a compressed JPEG/WebP suffices.

## Social / OG images

- Separate from UI: optimized crops under `/images/og/` (see `docs/seo/OG-IMAGE-STANDARD.md`).
- Budget: under ~200 KB per OG JPEG; dual 1200×630 + 1200×1200.
- Heavy heroes must not be used directly as `og:image`.

## Fonts

- `display=swap` on stylesheet fonts.
- Limit font families/weights on critical path.
- Prefer existing Fontshare / Google CSS approach unless migrating to `next/font` with measured benefit.

## JavaScript

- Prefer server components; client islands only for interaction.
- Avoid shipping large client libraries for static marketing sections.
- Code-split heavy tools (calculators, wizards) behind their routes.

## Caching

- Static marketing pages: cache-friendly build output on Vercel.
- Do not cache personalized form responses.
